hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19194","Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to me, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, from al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami, God willing, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The emigrant stays in Mecca after completing his rites three days. He said: Nothing was harder upon Ibn Uyayna than to say: Narrated to us."
"19195","Hushaym narrated to us: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Ibn al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami. My father said: Hushaym narrated it to us twice, once from Ibn al-Ala and once disconnected: That his father wrote to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and began with himself."
